      <div type="clause" n="83">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 83</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="83" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="366" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe þas laga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.14"/> wyrde, ðe se cingc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.15"/> hæfð nu ða<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.16"/> eallon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.17"/> mannon forgyfen, si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.5"/> he Denisc oððe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.star2"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.18"/> Englisc, beo he his weres<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.19"/> scyldig wið þone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.20"/> cingc.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.15"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="83" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="366" ed="#liebermann"/>Se ðe ðas lage wyrde, ðe se kyningc hæfð nu ða eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mannu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> forgyfen, seo he Denisc, sy he Engli[s]c<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.7"/>, beo he his weres scyldig wið ðone kyningc.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="83" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="366" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe þas laga wyrde, þe se cyning hæfð nu eallum mannon forgifen, sy he Denisc, sy he Englisc, beo he his weres scyldig wið þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.1"/> cyninc.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="83" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="367" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui leges istas apostatabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.9"/>, quas rex modo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.10"/> nobis omnibus indulsit, sit Dacus sit Anglicus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.11"/>, wérę suę reus sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.12"/> (erit) erga regem.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="83" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="367" ed="#liebermann"/>Quisquis has leges, quas rex modo omnibus hominibus concessit et statuit, sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.10-2"/> Anglus sit Danus, uiolauerit, persoluat regi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_83.lnote.oe.11-2"/> pretium sui ipsius.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="83" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="367" ed="#liebermann"/>[83] Quisquis autem hanc legem uiolauerit, quam rex nunc omnibus constituit, siue Danus siue Anglus, redempcionis sue reus sit erga regem.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="83" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="216" ed="#robertson"/>Se ðe ðas lage wyrde ðe se kyningc hæfð nu ða<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_83.robnote.fn.1"/> eallum mannum forgyfen, seo he Denisc sy he<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_83.robnote.fn.2"/> Engli[s]c<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_83.robnote.fn.3"/>, beo he his weres scyldig wið ðone kyningc.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="296" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And se ðe þas laga wyrde, ðe se cingc hæfð nu ða eallon mannon forgyfen, si he Denisc oððe Englisc, beo he his weres scyldig wið þone cingc.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="366" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_83.lnote.de.1"/> wer diese Satzungen verletzt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_83.lnote.de.2"/>, die der König eben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_83.lnote.de.3"/> nun allen Leuten gegeben hat, sei er Dänisch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_83.lnote.de.4"/>, sei er (oder <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) Englisch, sei der sein Wergeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_83.lnote.de.5"/> schuldig an den König.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever violates these statutes which the king has just now given to all people, whether he be Danish or (or, G) English, let him be liable for his wergild to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_83.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="217" ed="#robertson"/>He who violates the law which the king has now granted to all men, whether he be a Dane or an Englishman, shall forfeit his wergeld to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="474" ed="#whitelock"/>And he who violates these laws which the king has now given to all men, whether he be Danish or English, is to forfeit his wergild to the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="297" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And anyone, Danish or English, who violates the law which the king has granted to all of his people shall forfeit his wergild to the king.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="366"><ref target="clause:IIAs_25-2">II As 25.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II As. 25, 2</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="354"><label>follows model (reworded)</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_25-2">II As 25.2</ref> <quote>three clauses following the model of Æthelstan's summary punishing disobedience to the Grately code. But except for one phrase, the Cnut wording was entirely new</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="360"><label>modified (Table 5.4)</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_25-2">II As 25.2</ref> <quote>Table 5.4 row: 83–83:2 … II As 25:2 | Table 5.4, II Cn 83-83:2: II As 25:2</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II As 25.2.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 367, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">ða: omitted A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">367</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Cnuts Rest,</hi> 83—84, 6 <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The rest of Cnut, 83—84, 6, lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Englic</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Englic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">367</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">apostabit <hi rend="italic">K R Hk Hn</hi> 12, 4; <hi rend="italic">L Angl. in ECf.</hi> 32 <hi rend="italic">B</hi> ⁊</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">apostabit K R Hk Hn 12, 4; L Angl. in ECf. 32 B ⁊</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">367</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">n. m. <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">n. m. T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">367</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so KHn</hi> 34, 8; Anglus <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus KHn 34, 8; Anglus the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">367</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sit <hi rend="italic">KHk</hi>; <hi rend="italic">Hn L Angl.</hi>; erit <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sit KHk; Hn L Angl.; erit the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">lage <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lage Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyningc <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyningc Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lum mannum forgifen <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lum mannum forgifen Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sẏ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sẏ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si he <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi> [<hi rend="italic">ausser Cons.?</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si he the others [except Cons.?]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy he <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy he Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-re <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-re Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðonne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðonne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">367</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si A. si D. <hi rend="italic">Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si A. si D. Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">367</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">regit <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">regit Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B[...]en, und <hi rend="italic">eas</hi>[...] Quadr Arg 5; Hn 12[...]nnt II Ew 5 [?](aus Q) Lond ECf 32 B 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B[...]en, and <hi rend="italic">eas</hi>[...] Quadr Arg 5; Hn 12[...]nnt II Ew 5 [?] (from Q) Lond ECf 32 B 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">apostatare</hi> ‘vom Glauben abfallen’ Cyprian; transitiv bei Ducange nur hierher aus Q.—Nicht ein blosses Übertreten der Gesetze ist gemeint, sondern, wie II As 25, 2², ein trotziger Widerstand mit bewusster Absicht, die Regierung zu hemmen, wie Cn 1020, 9. (Andere Bed. <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 15, 3¹)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">apostatare</hi> ‘apostatize from the faith’ Cyprian; Ducange has it as transitive only here, from Q.—What is meant is not a mere transgression of the laws but, as in II As 25, 2², defiant resistance with the conscious intention of obstructing the government, as in Cn 1020, 9. (Another meaning <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 15, 3¹)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">þa</hi> fehlt <hi rend="smallcaps">A</hi>; <hi rend="italic">nu þa</hi> oft <hi rend="italic">modo, nunc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">þa</hi> missing in <hi rend="smallcaps">A</hi>; <hi rend="italic">nu þa</hi> often <hi rend="italic">modo, nunc</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl</hi>. Cn 1020, 9². Anders <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 17, 1¹</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf</hi>. Cn 1020, 9². Differently <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 17, 1¹</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_83.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gesetz 21b; Wergeld 30e</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gesetz 21b; Wergeld 30e</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_83.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and the two following, cf. II As. 25, 2.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_83.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">216</biblScope></bibl><label>ða</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_83.robnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">216</biblScope></bibl><label>he</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">D. oððe E.</hi> G.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_83.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">216</biblScope></bibl><label>Engli[s]c</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Englic</hi> B.</seg></note>
